{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[],"claim_ids":[],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:38Z","created_by_operation":"op_1ab179ee10ac4b19899376bde9da721f","id":"pg_19e171b1263359259489c6ce4f054666","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/langroid-langroid-pr-review-975-md-53c01d4e1a9e-c6ce4f054666.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_85901380582c5fe5a049f94960e8732d"],"title":"langroid/langroid/PR_REVIEW_975.md @ 53c01d4e1a9e","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:38Z","updated_by_operation":"op_1ab179ee10ac4b19899376bde9da721f"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_07cfa57fc6c9a1515ef4ed7bb048d6400d32f6afd273fd5629568d660376234e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"TableChatAgent accepts a dataset (file path, URL, or dataframe) and answers queries by having its LLM generate Pandas code via function-calling, which the agent's handler method executes."},{"claim_ids":["clm_3191dcf4143f79c4fb19ea234222695139f58cf52755d67df8f048376c2b19bc"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The multi-agent paradigm is inspired by the Actor model, and the framework does not use LangChain or any other LLM framework, aiming to work with practically any LLM."},{"claim_ids":["clm_3e52077b2ff559f444cf17922e622a22f36aeb92e4fad3c7aad1473fd83d4472"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"LLM configuration supports OpenAI models, any model behind an OpenAI-compatible API (e.g. \"ollama/mistral\"), and local models via chat_model strings such as \"local/localhost:8000\"."},{"claim_ids":["clm_3ec032ee593f0791bdc1b2469a1b5fa0d82c4459385576b8462ec324a22263c5"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A Claude Code plugin provides two skills: langroid:patterns for generating Langroid multi-agent code using proper design patterns, and langroid:add-pattern for recording newly learned patterns for future reference."},{"claim_ids":["clm_4ecd45cf5e980d9619f4da4a10d9a286eb069c826ba5feb85edbf7d2726aa029"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Supported vector stores include Qdrant cloud, Chroma (local storage, no API key needed), LanceDB, and Milvus; Milvus defaults to local storage at ./milvus.db, and Milvus Lite is unavailable on Windows."},{"claim_ids":["clm_63e23efd773529940518f1fb1ce334167c0f19ea98a08093c016937cdda4a626"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Langroid is a Python framework for building LLM applications where users set up Agents equipped with optional components (LLM, vector-store, tools/functions) that collaborate by exchanging messages."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6ef3ce00978788541270b7a15de8d3f87b6d107643f1ed25178f001d2b6e9c23"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"DocChatAgent supports chat with documents by sharding, embedding, storing in a vector DB, and retrieval-augmented answer generation, configured via DocChatAgentConfig with doc_paths and a vecdb setting."},{"claim_ids":["clm_73ab4c005b47f9449826fc998b23b84346f099d698f87957cbe10bc2766a1e9d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README states the prompts and instructions have been tested to work well with GPT-4 (and to some extent GPT-4o); other LLMs may yield inferior results unless prompts or the multi-agent setup are adjusted."},{"claim_ids":["clm_80fdc521582a18fe7e7fdd580f8894a842527d41b76ecb654c9c982dcd58771a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Tools are defined by subclassing ToolMessage with a request field naming the handling agent method, a purpose description, and typed arguments; agents enable tools via enable_message, and Pydantic validation errors are sent back to the LLM for self-correction."},{"claim_ids":["clm_82a9b318f87f6bab08b904e3ceddbf455d44f7628120e764f98a211bcb9096a2"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The Agent class encapsulates LLM conversation state plus an optional vector-store and tools, acts as a message transformer, and by default provides three responder methods corresponding to LLM, Agent, and User."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8e3b75c74fb8d812792a7023149e3e7b5cff8f9663d6aa8bad5c08d4e7ebd56d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"LLM API responses can be cached via Redis or Momento (CACHE_TYPE=momento); if Redis settings are absent, Langroid falls back to a pure-Python in-memory cache via Fakeredis."},{"claim_ids":["clm_b13ffd944d0f7dc057cb755b8c52656adb56f47168a16b9f93cac31770e969a6"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Langroid requires Python 3.11+ and is installable from PyPI, with optional extras including hf-embeddings, doc-chat, db, postgres, and all (the latter increasing install size and startup time)."},{"claim_ids":["clm_be4165d8851873e314cff6b0f4875327711e4547bc9e5555bfee0b296c128b57"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Langroid includes an MCP tool adapter that converts an MCP server's tools into Langroid ToolMessage instances so any LLM agent can leverage MCP servers."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f6b6bb1b173887469c6bc272f026fd36266b6eb3c1e241aa55ca6297870462a3"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A Task wraps an Agent, manages iteration over the agent's responder methods, and orchestrates multi-agent interaction via hierarchical, recursive task delegation; sub-tasks are treated as additional responders used round-robin after the agent's own responders."}],"claim_ids":["clm_07cfa57fc6c9a1515ef4ed7bb048d6400d32f6afd273fd5629568d660376234e","clm_3191dcf4143f79c4fb19ea234222695139f58cf52755d67df8f048376c2b19bc","clm_3e52077b2ff559f444cf17922e622a22f36aeb92e4fad3c7aad1473fd83d4472","clm_3ec032ee593f0791bdc1b2469a1b5fa0d82c4459385576b8462ec324a22263c5","clm_4ecd45cf5e980d9619f4da4a10d9a286eb069c826ba5feb85edbf7d2726aa029","clm_63e23efd773529940518f1fb1ce334167c0f19ea98a08093c016937cdda4a626","clm_6ef3ce00978788541270b7a15de8d3f87b6d107643f1ed25178f001d2b6e9c23","clm_73ab4c005b47f9449826fc998b23b84346f099d698f87957cbe10bc2766a1e9d","clm_80fdc521582a18fe7e7fdd580f8894a842527d41b76ecb654c9c982dcd58771a","clm_82a9b318f87f6bab08b904e3ceddbf455d44f7628120e764f98a211bcb9096a2","clm_8e3b75c74fb8d812792a7023149e3e7b5cff8f9663d6aa8bad5c08d4e7ebd56d","clm_b13ffd944d0f7dc057cb755b8c52656adb56f47168a16b9f93cac31770e969a6","clm_be4165d8851873e314cff6b0f4875327711e4547bc9e5555bfee0b296c128b57","clm_f6b6bb1b173887469c6bc272f026fd36266b6eb3c1e241aa55ca6297870462a3"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:38Z","created_by_operation":"op_1ab179ee10ac4b19899376bde9da721f","id":"pg_2dc800252f91564780728cc8f4c92985","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/langroid-langroid-readme-md-53c01d4e1a9e-8cc8f4c92985.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_962ebf85bc9053058727328062747ed1"],"title":"langroid/langroid/README.md @ 53c01d4e1